BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:QEN Open House Fundraiser
DTSTART:20261130T180000
DTEND:20261130T180000
UID:0039ed95049de747b83fe0a4e9aabb7a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Join us Monday\, November 30 at 6pm for our QEN Open House &am
 p\; Fundraiser! Meet our founding committee\, hear what we’re building f
 or 2027 and help fund the launch of our website and queer business directo
 ry\, a place to discover\, connect with and support our community. Enjoy a
  complimentary welcome drink and snacks Enter our raffle for amazing prize
 s donated by our community Mingle with fellow queer entrepreneurs and make
  some new connections Whether you’re nurturing an idea\, running an esta
 blished business or finding your next direction\, you belong here. Allies\
 , this is your invitation to show up and invest in queer community\, too! 
 Tickets: FREE for queer entrepreneurs | $20 for allies The Queer Entrepren
 eur Network is rooted in community\, connection and reciprocity: sharing w
 hat we know\, showing up for one another and building opportunities for qu
 eer businesses to thrive. Together\, we’re creating the support network 
 we want to be part of. Come meet your community. Help build what comes nex
 t. Reserve your ticket and share this with someone who should be in the ro
 om! ‍
LOCATION:Three Dollar Bill\, 1592 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/qen-open-house-fundraiser
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Entrepreneurs: Open House &amp\; Fundraiser
DTSTART:20261130T180000
DTEND:20261130T180000
UID:c8f156478179c3916c6b043e5578808e@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:BIG PLANS. BIG COMMUNITY. BIG QUEER ENERGY. You’re invited t
 o the Queer Entrepreneur Network OPEN HOUSE &amp\; FUNDRAISER! What starte
 d as a desire to feel less alone in entrepreneurship has grown into a comm
 unity rooted in connection\, collaboration and reciprocity. And we’re ju
 st getting started! We’ve got BIG plans for 2027\, and we want YOU to he
 lp us build what’s next! WHAT TO EXPECT: Meet the QEN Founding Committee
  and learn about our vision for 2027 Mingle with queer entrepreneurs\, all
 ies and community supporters Enjoy a complimentary welcome drink\, snacks 
 and entertainment Enter our community raffle featuring incredible prizes f
 rom local businesses! 📅 MONDAY\, NOVEMBER 30 | 6PM 📍 Three Dollar Bi
 ll | 1592 Queen St. W. 🎟️ FREE for queer entrepreneurs | $20 for alli
 es &amp\; supporters We’re raising funds to launch our website and queer
 -owned business directory\, creating more opportunities for connection\, v
 isibility and growth. Can’t attend but want to support? We’re acceptin
 g raffle prize donations and monetary contributions! DM us to get involved
 . Community doesn’t build itself. It takes participation\, commitment an
 d people showing up for one another. That’s reciprocity in action. Queer
  entrepreneurship is worth investing in. Queer community is worth showing 
 up for. Tickets at the link in bio! Tag someone who should be in the room!
  #QueerEntrepreneurNetwork #QENToronto #QueerEntrepreneurs #SupportQueerBu
 siness #QueerCommunity ‍
LOCATION:Three Dollar Bill\, 1592 Queen Street West
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/queer-entrepreneurs-open-house-fundraiser
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:I Can Do What I Want Now
DTSTART:20261201T190000
DTEND:20261201T190000
UID:711b016b58469a7f0396758bb976a711@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. In this Qu
 eer Death Salon\, Carta Monir roots us in her own experience of coming out
  as trans around the time that her mom was diagnosed with terminal cancer\
 , and the way her mother&#x27\;s death allowed her to express her womanhoo
 d in ways that she previously thought were impossible.. Participants will 
 explore the authenticity and permission for queer expression that can be c
 reated at the end of a loved one&#x27\;s life\, and after. 18+ imagery and
  themes will be integrated in this salon. Carta Monir is a writer\, visual
  artist\, and sex worker living in Michigan. She was an artist in residenc
 e at the Tom of Finland Foundation\, and her work has been exhibited and s
 creened internationally. Her work deals with pain\, disability\, trauma\, 
 and perseverance. https://cartamonir.com/ Photo credit: Cody Sells ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/i-can-do-what-i-want-now
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
