BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:This Will Go On Your Permanent Record
DTSTART:20261208T190000
DTEND:20261208T190000
UID:97204bc54b5564a12523cef2023a0569@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Queer Death Salon is a virtual community space for all 2SLGBTQ
 IA+ people to come together to discuss death\, dying and grief. Badly Lick
 ed Bear will lead participants in a discussion on scars\, wounds\, illness
 \, and disability. Like trees in a rainforest\, our bodies are simultaneou
 sly places of growth and decay\; parallel forces that define and carry us 
 and guide us towards the final disposition. We&#x27\;ll explore what it fe
 els like to experience our progress towards death\, in particular the perm
 anent changes to our bodies\, minds\, and spirits that come as out physica
 l bodies continue to grow and change. Let&#x27\;s gather and share reflect
 ions on the ways we live our lives\; fully\, and in part\, as people who o
 ften feel like part of ourselves\, or that part of ourselves that we once 
 knew is now gone\, or with the reminders of the experiences that have left
  their marks on us. Our bodies\, in sickness and health\, growing\, changi
 ng\, and dying\, are the archive - the permanent record - of our lives. Th
 ey not only tell a story\, they determine the stories that are possible fo
 r us to live and tell\, as the reality that we have walked close to and wi
 th death all our lives is slowly revealed to us. (FOR MORE INFO SEE TICKET
  LINK PROVIDED)
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/this-will-go-on-your-permanent-record
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Glitter in the Archives
DTSTART:20261209T180000
DTEND:20261209T180000
UID:5fddfc2d8a10899c10be7e2eef3ce664@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Glitter in the Archives: reference materials for re-creation I
 n this talk\, Ian Danger Capstick traces his practice of quilting using Th
 e ArQuives’ and other archival photographic collections as reference. He
  recreates protest signs and banners\, ephemeral objects often made to las
 t only an afternoon\, as quilted objects you can hold today. His talk intr
 oduces artists and thinkers who have influenced his work and who invented\
 , fabricated and quilted their own queer ancestry when the record came up 
 empty. Glitter here is literal (polyester\, metallic thread\, a conservato
 r’s nightmare)\, metaphorical (evidence that refuses to behave) and fina
 lly a call to action: create sparkle\, save your ephemera\, support your c
 ommunity archivist and treat our local archives and museums as essential i
 nfrastructure. December 9\, 2026 6:00PM - 7:30PM The ArQuives\, Toronto PW
 YC\, 5$ suggested\, Registration Required: arquives.ca/event/glitter-in-th
 e-archives ‍
LOCATION:The ArQuives\, 34 Isabella Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/glitter-in-the-archives
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
