BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queen Out - Queer &amp\; Fem Open Mic Comedy!
DTSTART:20261213T183000
DTEND:20261213T183000
UID:ac22234b584ed7bf0cd9a109f8a5ff76@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:An evening of open mic comedy for the girls\, gays\, and theys
 ! Looking for stage time to try out your silly lil jokes? Want to hang wit
 h other fem and / or queer comedians? Just want to belly laugh and cure yo
 ur Sunday Scaries? Well you are in luck! Join us for Queen Out Open Mic Co
 medy! This mic is all about a comfy\, inclusive\, and fun live comedy expe
 rience for women and 2SLQBTQIA+ folks. Sign up starts at 6 pm\, with sign 
 up on a first come\, first serve basis. The show starts promptly at 6 30 p
 m\, and will run to approximately 8 - 8 30 pm (depending on the number of 
 sign ups). This mic is open to anyone that identifies as a woman\, fem\, a
 nd / or member of the 2SLGBTQIA+ community. Sorry cis het dude comics - th
 is one&#x27\;s not for you. You are welcome to perform\, attend as an audi
 ence member to support fem and queer comedy\, or both!! Audience entry by 
 donation ($5 recommended\, donate what you can). Please note that this eve
 nt is an open mic and not a professional\, ticketed comedy show. We do our
  best to keep the quality high and the vibes good\, but please know the na
 ture of open mic comedy means there may be an odd &quot\;miss&quot\;. The 
 fine print: 5 minute sets\, &quot\;warning light&quot\; at 4 minutes No pu
 rchase is required on top of your entry-by-donation\, but please support t
 he amazing venue if you can. There are a range of nonalcoholic and alcohol
 ic beverages for purchase as well as light food The venue is fully accessi
 ble for mobility aid users including communal and single stall gender neut
 ral washrooms at-grade All ages welcome but parental / guardian company is
  recommended for younger performers All are welcome to watch / support thi
 s event\, including cisgender heterosexual men\, but performance spaces ar
 e open only to fem and / or queer folx We will do our best to get everyone
  up who wants to perform\, but we also need to be out of the venue before 
 our allotted time ends and want to keep the show length manageable and ple
 asant. This means we may have to cap or limit the list and / or reduce set
  times if we have more perfomers than expected. Please arrive as early as 
 possible to maximize your chances of getting on. Community guidelines are 
 in place for this show and will be discussed at the top. This includes no 
 &quot\;punching down&quot\;\, no &quot\;isms&quot\; or phobias\, and no ag
 gressive crowd work. This mic is hosted and produced by a queer\, nonbinar
 y comedian who takes this seriously AF\, and who is committed to keeping t
 he vibes cute and inclusive. If content of a performance isn&#x27\;t align
 ed with the guidelines\, the set will be ended early. We all want a sexy\,
  healthy time! You are totally welcome to wear a mask. If you are feeling 
 sick\, please stay home! Questions? Want to come out but are a lil nervous
 ? Totally feel free to reach out to the producer Anna Sebastien on Instagr
 am at @annasebastiencomedy - its all about community! ‍
LOCATION:Society Clubhouse\, 967 College Street
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/queen-out---queer-fem-open-mic-comedy
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
