BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sapphic Bacchus at Birdhaus
DTSTART:20261219T200000
DTEND:20261219T200000
UID:6d1bd10e34a07905025c5b1fd52e2804@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:In Greek mythology\, maenads were the female followers of Dion
 ysus and the most significant members of his retinue. Their name literally
  translates as &#x27\;raving ones&#x27\;. Maenads were known as Bassarids\
 , Bacchae\, in Roman mythology after the penchant of the equivalent Roman 
 god\, Bacchus\, to wear a bassaris or fox skin. Often the maenads were por
 trayed as inspired by Dionysus into a state of ecstatic frenzy through a c
 ombination of dancing\, wine and revelry. During these rites\, the maenads
  would dress in fawn skins and carry a thyrsus\, a long stick wrapped in i
 vy or vine leaves and tipped with a pine cone. They would weave ivy wreath
 s around their heads\, and often handle or wear snakes. Special wine cockt
 ails for the night. Join the Maenads for a night and be part of a sapphic 
 Bacchus takeover of Birdhaus. Dress in your best Greek revelry. This is a 
 play party exclusively for women\, trans\, non-binary\, and two-spirit fol
 x. You do not have to identify as “sapphic” if it does not fit\; the o
 nly limitation on attendance is that cis men are not permitted in the spac
 e. CIS MEN ARE NOT PERMITTED TO ATTEND THIS EVENT. We have more events com
 ing up that will be open to everyone! Follow @salemburnsevents to stay up 
 to date. ‍
LOCATION:Birdhaus\, 1233 Queen Street West Rear ( the big pink building!)
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/sapphic-bacchus-at-birdhaus
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
